From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: fix: misaligned epoll_event read in MessagePumpEpoll DCHECK

epoll_event is packed on x86-64, so its 8-byte `data` member sits at
offset 4. In the array that epoll_wait() fills, every other element's
`data.ptr` is therefore misaligned. ~EpollEventEntry() checks
`DCHECK_EQ(this, active_event->data.ptr)`, and DCHECK_EQ() takes its
operands by const reference, so this binds a reference to a misaligned
pointer, which is undefined behavior.

This destructor runs with `active_event` set when a handler for one
ready descriptor unregisters another descriptor from the same
epoll_wait() batch, which is common while sockets and IPC channels are
torn down at shutdown. Builds with the UBSan alignment check and
DCHECKs on report it (and abort with halt_on_error=1), for example from
net::UDPSocketPosix::Close() and net::SpdySession::~SpdySession() in
the network service.

Compare a copy of the pointer instead.

This patch should be upstreamed.

diff --git a/base/message_loop/message_pump_epoll.cc b/base/message_loop/message_pump_epoll.cc
index eb45299d036d8b974177b4fe5b1d43ba2ca6fdcd..bd87e79ce13f625d8988ec1baf2cd15c38a04216 100644
--- a/base/message_loop/message_pump_epoll.cc
+++ b/base/message_loop/message_pump_epoll.cc
@@ -680,7 +680,10 @@ MessagePumpEpoll::EpollEventEntry::EpollEventEntry(int fd) : fd(fd) {}
 
 MessagePumpEpoll::EpollEventEntry::~EpollEventEntry() {
   if (active_event) {
-    DCHECK_EQ(this, active_event->data.ptr);
+    // epoll_event is packed on x86-64, so `data.ptr` is not always 8-byte
+    // aligned. DCHECK_EQ() takes its operands by reference, so compare a copy:
+    // binding a reference to a misaligned pointer is undefined behavior.
+    DCHECK_EQ(this, static_cast<void*>(active_event->data.ptr));
     active_event->data.ptr = nullptr;
   }
 }
